BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How Did We Get Here: Stories of Migration and Home | Exhibition Op
 ening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261022T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261022T170000
UID:chamber-e.4410.1367744@moabchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:We will conclude 2026 with a community exhibition inviting art
 ists and makers\, both local and from afar\, to submit work in any medium 
 under the theme: "How Did We Get Here? Stories of Migration and Home."\nWe
  encourage you to explore themes of movement\, connection across time\, mi
 gration routes\, and the idea of home. Consider drawing from your own fami
 ly history—journeys to and from the Moab Valley\, throughout Utah\, acro
 ss the United States\, or around the world.\nWe invite creators of all bac
 kgrounds to submit work for an exhibition celebrating diverse interpretati
 ons of movement and home\, with all entries reviewed by a community commit
 tee and the Museum reserving the right to decline submissions that fall ou
 tside our mission or disparage others.\nAbout the Semiquincentennial:\nThe
  semiquincentennial is a chance for everyone to feel a part of this major 
 milestone in our nation. We can celebrate courage\, liberty\, and sacrific
 e\, while also reckoning with difficult truths. By fostering a sense of be
 longing and coming together with our local communities\, we can ensure tha
 t Utahns of all ages and backgrounds see themselves in American history.\n
 This is our last exhibit for the year commemorating America's 250th! Thank
 s to all who have supported the work of the Museum\, our mission to share 
 stories\, and for being part of something special here in Moab\, UT.
LOCATION:118 E Center Streeet Moab UT 84532
URL:https://business.moabchamber.com/eventcalendar/Details/how-did-we-get-
 here-stories-of-migration-and-home-exhibition-opening-1613830?sourceTypeId
 =Hub
X-SOURCE:Moab Area Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Living Rivers Expedition: Cataract Canyon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260708T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260711T180000
UID:chamber-e.4410.1460287@moabchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:Cataract Canyon through Canyonlands National Park is a journey
  into a spectacular\, remote wilderness. This quality multi-faceted advent
 ure is the ideal balance of serenity\, fascination\, and exhilaration – 
 it will elevate your life. And this year\, we are proud to partner with bo
 th Sheri Griffith Adventures\, who is outfitting and organizing this exclu
 sive Cataract Canyon trip\, and John Weisheit of Living Rivers\, who will 
 be the Naturalist on this four-day float.\nJohn Weisheit cofounded Living 
 Rivers\, based in Moab\, Utah\, in 2000. In 2002\, John became a member of
  the Waterkeeper Alliance and serves this international organization as th
 e Colorado Riverkeeper. He has been a professional river guide and interpr
 eter of natural and human history since 1980. Since 1990\, John has comple
 ted about 75 science-based expeditions to assess the long-term impacts of 
 water and energy development on the Colorado River\, with a special emphas
 is on the Colorado Plateau. Secure your spot on this exclusive and limited
 -capacity trip HERE: https://go.theflybook.com/book/1669/EntityConfig/4440
 5
LOCATION:118 E Center Streeet Moab UT 84532
URL:https://business.moabchamber.com/eventcalendar/Details/living-rivers-e
 xpedition-cataract-canyon-1729598?sourceTypeId=Hub
X-SOURCE:Moab Area Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
