BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moab History 101: Open Session Spring 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T200000
UID:chamber-e.4410.1434051@moabchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:Moab History 101 was designed to introduce local guides and re
 creation-industry employees to Moab’s history through the stories\, arti
 facts\, and primary resources available at the Moab Museum. Facilitated in
  collaboration with History Moab founder\, Blaine Reniger\, this Open Sess
 ion of Moab History 101\, which takes place from 6-8 pm on Tuesday\, May 2
 6th at the Museum\, invites local guides\, history buffs\, and curious com
 munity members alike to join us for a night of learning and story sharing.
  This program will include an in-depth guided gallery tour of the Moab Mus
 eum and an additional presentation on topics of particular interest\, usin
 g historic photos\, oral histories\, and items from the Museum collection.
  The cost of the open session is $40. Email the Museum's Director of Progr
 ams at megan@moabmuseum.org for more information and to secure your spot o
 n scholarship for free.
LOCATION:118 E Center Streeet Moab UT 84532
URL:https://business.moabchamber.com/eventcalendar/Details/moab-history-10
 1-open-session-spring-2026-1697547?sourceTypeId=Hub
X-SOURCE:Moab Area Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
